    rdfs:label "rock"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Rock is a natural solid aggregate of one or more minerals or mineraloids that constitutes a fundamental component of the Earth's crust. In Pre-Salt petroleum geology, rocks are critical as reservoir facies, such as microbialites and carbonates, or as seals, like evaporites, with their physical properties, including porosity and permeability, dictating their capacity to store and transmit hydrocarbons."@en ;
